    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13.7">
        <head>Cn 1018 13.7</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#kennedy" n="13.7" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="76" ed="#kennedy"/>And gif man ænig lic of rihtre scriftscire. elles hwar lecge. gelæste man þone sawlsceat swa ðeah into ðam mynstre. þe hit to hyrde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="216" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gif man ænig lic of rihtre scriftscire elles hwar lecge, gelæste man þone sawlsceat swa ðeah into ðam mynstre þe hit to hyrde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#kennedy" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="76" ed="#kennedy"/>And if any body is buried elsewhere than in the right parish, the payment should nevertheless be made to the church to which it belongs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="217" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if any person’s body is buried other than in its proper parish, the dues should still be paid to the church to which he belonged.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="314"><ref target="clause:IIEg_2-3">II Eg 2.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="314"><ref target="clause:IIEg_5-1">II Eg 5.1–3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="314"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_8-1">III Eg 8.1–3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="24"><ref target="clause:VAtr_12-1">V Atr 12.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><ref target="clause:ICn_13-1">I Cn 13.1</ref></note>
      </div>
